    "answer": {
      "short": "$$\\lvert x\\rvert=\\sqrt{x^2}$$\n$$\\lvert x\\rvert=\\begin{cases}x&\\text{if }x\\ge0,\\\\-x&\\text{if }x<0.\\end{cases}$$",
      "worked": "The distance of $x$ from zero is $x$ when $x\\ge0$ and $-x$ when $x<0$:\n$$\\lvert x\\rvert=\\begin{cases}x&\\text{if }x\\ge0,\\\\-x&\\text{if }x<0.\\end{cases}$$\nThe nonnegative square root of $x^2$ gives the same value, so equivalently\n$$\\lvert x\\rvert=\\sqrt{x^2}.$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
